  "id": "Compound::DB01056 - Gene::6334",
  "verbalization": "Tocainide appears to interact with voltage-gated sodium channels through a shared mechanism involving participation in sodium channel activity. The evidence suggests that Tocainide binds to specific sodium channel subunits—Scn7a, Scn3a, and Scn10a—each of which participates in voltage-gated sodium channel activity. This activity is then linked to Scn8a, indicating a potential pathway where Tocainide may influence Scn8a through these intermediate subunits. The cumulative scores from the three paths suggest a consistent interaction pattern, though the exact mechanism of how Tocainide affects Scn8a remains partially inferred. The relationship is supported by a network of binding and participation, but the precise role of Tocainide in modulating Scn8a's function remains an area of further investigation.",
